[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2458048797","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/139789#issuecomment-2458048797","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/139789","id":2458048797,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z86Sgtkd","user":{"login":"bdhirsh","id":16311747,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzExNzQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16311747?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh","html_url":"https://github.com/bdhirsh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-05T20:01:37Z","updated_at":"2024-11-05T20:01:37Z","body":"I can think of a few options (none of which seem particularly appealing):\r\n\r\n(1) Whenever we have a graph with an input mutation, add negative guards that guard on the fact that the mutated input does not alias any other inputs. This has the downside that this guard would need to run **whenever* we have a graph with an input mutation, and it needs to check aliasing with every other graph input, making it potentially expensive\r\n\r\n(2) kill the \"mutation + aliasing\" case that we support in AOTAutograd. This is potentially BC breaking, but my hope is that it is extremely rare for people to run into this case, and it should (generally) be fixable by tweaking where you slap compile on your model. I've been hoping for a while that we can do this\r\n\r\n(3) accept this silent correctness today (which, given the assumption that \"multiple graph inputs that alias each other and mutate\" is rare, might be a very rare case for someone to run into)","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2458048797/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2458063654","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/139789#issuecomment-2458063654","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/139789","id":2458063654,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z86SgxMm","user":{"login":"bdhirsh","id":16311747,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzExNzQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16311747?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh","html_url":"https://github.com/bdhirsh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-05T20:10:41Z","updated_at":"2024-11-05T20:10:41Z","body":"Oh an option (4) would be to guard on storage offset, which we are evidently not doing in the above repro. IIRC we don't want to do this though, because inductor generally doesn't really need to guard on data pointer","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/2458063654/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3412256299","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/139789#issuecomment-3412256299","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/139789","id":3412256299,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z87LYuYr","user":{"login":"bdhirsh","id":16311747,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzExNzQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16311747?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh","html_url":"https://github.com/bdhirsh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bdhirsh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-16T18:25:25Z","updated_at":"2025-10-16T18:25:25Z","body":"@bdhirsh to chat with a few other folks (@Lucaskabela) to agree on a design","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/3412256299/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_gi